WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
If your prep is SUPREP, this video will walk you through exactly how to

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.760
take it, just follow along step-by-step.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.200
Your bowel prep kit comes with two small bottles and a mixing container.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.840
You'll use one bottle the evening before your procedure and the second bottle

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:14.760
the morning of.

6
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.500
You'll also need water.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.400
For your first dose between 5 and 6 p.m. the evening before your colonoscopy,

8
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.500
pour the entire contents of the first bottle into the mixing container provided

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:25.500
.

10
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.730
Fill the container with water to the 16 ounces fill line and drink the entire

11
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:30.400
amount.

12
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.070
After you finish, continue to drink 16 to 32 ounces of clear liquids until you go

13
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:35.700
to bed.

14
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.100
Remember, do not drink red, orange, blue or purple liquids.

15
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.020
For your second dose, 7 hours before your procedure time, pour the entire

16
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.800
contents of the second bottle into the mixing container.

17
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.600
Fill with water to the 16 ounces fill line and drink the entire amount.

18
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.050
After finishing the second dose, drink an additional 32 ounces of water within 1

19
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:54.600
hour.

20
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.600
Do not have any liquids at all within 4 hours of your procedure.

21
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.400
This part is really important.

22
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.320
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed even if you're already

23
00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.600
passing clear liquid.

24
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.900
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

25
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.200
the clearest view during your procedure.

26
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.330
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

27
00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.400
of us wants that.

28
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.100
Staying hydrated throughout the process is key.

29
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.100
Make sure you're drinking plenty of clear liquids between your doses.

30
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.220
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

31
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.700
a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

32
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.700
That's it, you've got this.

33
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.900
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

34
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.900
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

35
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:37.900
We're here to help.
